01:57:46.510 --> 01:57:48.910
Dr. Rawiri, welcome to the Health Committee.

1800
01:57:49.570 --> 01:57:52.950
We have you here for five minutes. You may leave us time for questions if you want,

1801
01:57:53.010 --> 01:57:55.110
but I'll hand that time to you now. Thank you.

1802
01:57:56.550 --> 01:58:00.030
Kia ora. Tena tatou. Ko Rawiri McRee-Jensen tēnei.

1803
01:58:00.040 --> 01:58:02.770
He uri ahau nō Ngāti Hinerangi, Ngāti Raukawa.

1804
01:58:03.630 --> 01:58:04.950
I'm a general practitioner,

1805
01:58:06.030 --> 01:58:09.290
and I've been in general practice for more than 25 years.

1806
01:58:09.560 --> 01:58:12.290
Mostly in high-needs communities in South Auckland

1807
01:58:13.150 --> 01:58:17.050
and currently on the East Coast. And I appear today in front of you in my

1808
01:58:17.110 --> 01:58:17.950
personal capacity,

1809
01:58:19.230 --> 01:58:20.990
and in support of this bill.

1810
01:58:22.230 --> 01:58:23.430
My first

1811
01:58:24.790 --> 01:58:28.470
comment for you is that overdose is a medical

1812
01:58:28.510 --> 01:58:29.150
emergency,

1813
01:58:30.790 --> 01:58:34.090
and it should be treated like any other medical emergency.

1814
01:58:34.150 --> 01:58:35.950
When somebody collapses with a heart attack,

1815
01:58:37.050 --> 01:58:38.450
people around them call 111

1816
01:58:39.730 --> 01:58:43.230
without hesitating. But when somebody collapses from an overdose,

1817
01:58:45.070 --> 01:58:48.890
people around them might hesitate, and they weigh up

1818
01:58:48.930 --> 01:58:52.270
whether calling for help will bring police

1819
01:58:52.330 --> 01:58:56.059
attention as well as paramedics for themselves, but also with a

1820
01:58:56.110 --> 01:58:58.210
person who's in distress in front of them.

1821
01:58:59.130 --> 01:59:03.050
And so that hesitation is measured in minutes, and in an overdose,

1822
01:59:03.270 --> 01:59:05.010
minutes are the whole game.

1823
01:59:06.410 --> 01:59:09.090
Respiratory depression is reversible.

1824
01:59:09.690 --> 01:59:10.910
Naloxone works.

1825
01:59:11.870 --> 01:59:15.350
Basic airway support works. And all of that works

1826
01:59:15.470 --> 01:59:18.990
if the person gets that help in time.

1827
01:59:20.470 --> 01:59:23.910
Other medical emergencies don't carry a legal penalty for calling an

1828
01:59:23.990 --> 01:59:27.830
ambulance, and this bill simply gives people who overdose, and the people who

1829
01:59:27.870 --> 01:59:28.320
help them,

1830
01:59:29.230 --> 01:59:32.900
the same access to emergency care that every other New Zealander already

1831
01:59:32.950 --> 01:59:35.790
has, and that's not a radical proposition.

1832
01:59:36.010 --> 01:59:39.250
I think that's an important contribution.

1833
01:59:41.010 --> 01:59:43.910
Secondly, I'd say the current law

1834
01:59:44.590 --> 01:59:47.470
incentivizes patients to not disclose

1835
01:59:47.870 --> 01:59:51.710
to their GPs, and this

1836
01:59:51.770 --> 01:59:55.650
is a quieter harm, but I see it in my consulting

1837
01:59:55.690 --> 01:59:59.430
room every week, and criminalization teaches people

1838
01:59:59.670 --> 02:00:02.610
to conceal their substance abuse from police. Yep.

1839
02:00:03.290 --> 02:00:07.230
But also from paramedics, from emergency departments, from their

1840
02:00:07.250 --> 02:00:07.930
own GP.

1841
02:00:09.070 --> 02:00:12.730
And when a patient has trouble telling me about what they're actually

1842
02:00:12.790 --> 02:00:15.250
taking, that makes it harder for me to do my job.

1843
02:00:16.250 --> 02:00:19.530
That's true in a general sense. I would notice that

1844
02:00:19.970 --> 02:00:23.850
patients who've got renal failure, I really want to work actively to make sure that

1845
02:00:23.890 --> 02:00:27.790
they can tell me about what other natural remedies they might be taking.

1846
02:00:27.870 --> 02:00:30.350
If there's any disquiet or

1847
02:00:31.210 --> 02:00:34.850
concern about sharing that, then it makes it harder for me to look after them.

1848
02:00:36.030 --> 02:00:39.570
And in the context

1849
02:00:39.770 --> 02:00:43.250
of substance use, it's really important that

1850
02:00:44.330 --> 02:00:48.180
we are creating a safe space for patients to talk to their

1851
02:00:48.650 --> 02:00:49.510
health professionals.

1852
02:00:51.190 --> 02:00:54.910
I prescribe medicines that interact with substances, and I need to know

1853
02:00:54.990 --> 02:00:56.150
about what they're taking.

1854
02:00:57.170 --> 02:00:57.390
So,

1855
02:00:58.270 --> 02:01:02.230
missing an early window for treating drug dependence is an

1856
02:01:02.270 --> 02:01:02.570
issue,

1857
02:01:03.450 --> 02:01:07.370
and it makes it harder to offer naloxone to households

1858
02:01:07.410 --> 02:01:10.850
that need it because those households might not disclose.

1859
02:01:11.770 --> 02:01:14.850
And I think ambulance officers will tell you a similar thing, that they arrive at

1860
02:01:14.870 --> 02:01:18.190
an overdose and people at the scene

1861
02:01:18.310 --> 02:01:20.810
are reluctant to talk about what was taken.

1862
02:01:21.090 --> 02:01:24.990
So that treatment is starting blind, and it takes extra

1863
02:01:25.050 --> 02:01:28.930
effort to work with whānau. So honesty is a

1864
02:01:28.950 --> 02:01:32.330
clinical safety issue, and a law that punishes

1865
02:01:32.390 --> 02:01:33.010
disclosure

1866
02:01:33.990 --> 02:01:37.630
will predictably produce silence, and that silence will produce

1867
02:01:37.690 --> 02:01:38.530
avoidable deaths.

1868
02:01:39.670 --> 02:01:42.550
And so this bill, I think, starts to dismantle that.

1869
02:01:44.370 --> 02:01:48.350
And then the final comment from me would be thinking about the

1870
02:01:49.110 --> 02:01:52.810
burden of fatal overdose is not evenly spread in our

1871
02:01:52.830 --> 02:01:56.770
society. Māori die at overdose roughly twice the rate of non-Māori.

1872
02:01:57.650 --> 02:01:59.110
And I think

1873
02:02:00.730 --> 02:02:04.419
it's important to notice that Māori communities have good historical

1874
02:02:04.510 --> 02:02:08.370
reasons to expect that calling for help doesn't always bring

1875
02:02:08.630 --> 02:02:11.460
help. It brings enforcement. And so that fear barrier

1876
02:02:13.350 --> 02:02:16.630
sits disproportionately for Māori communities.

1877
02:02:17.550 --> 02:02:19.550
And so this bill is important because it

1878
02:02:20.390 --> 02:02:22.590
supports equity in my view.

1879
02:02:24.474 --> 02:02:28.454
In closing, I'd say you'll hear from people directly affected by

1880
02:02:28.834 --> 02:02:32.034
overdose, and mothers who have lost children.

1881
02:02:32.974 --> 02:02:34.314
And as a clinician,

1882
02:02:35.174 --> 02:02:37.214
my ask is pretty simple, it's

1883
02:02:38.574 --> 02:02:39.614
please pass this bill.

1884
02:02:40.774 --> 02:02:44.034
That's all I've got to say, and I don't know, we might have a

1885
02:02:44.294 --> 02:02:45.134
question. Over.

1886
02:02:47.134 --> 02:02:50.334
Okay. Thank you, Dr. Rawiri. Very good to have you here.

1887
02:02:50.394 --> 02:02:51.414
We are at time.

1888
02:02:52.554 --> 02:02:52.614
Oh.

1889
02:02:52.624 --> 02:02:53.193
Oh, no, sorry.

1890
02:02:53.494 --> 02:02:53.894
Yes, I want-

1891
02:02:54.074 --> 02:02:54.464
Go for it

1892
02:02:54.474 --> 02:02:57.054
... thank you, Doctor. I just have one very quick question.

1893
02:02:57.974 --> 02:03:00.514
We're hearing a lot in terms of the

1894
02:03:00.574 --> 02:03:04.554
hesitation and the delay that has greater

1895
02:03:05.314 --> 02:03:05.614
medical

1896
02:03:07.574 --> 02:03:11.214
results for the patient who has overdosed,

1897
02:03:11.574 --> 02:03:13.054
and fear being one of the

1898
02:03:14.034 --> 02:03:17.554
factors for that hesitation, criminal prosecution

1899
02:03:17.654 --> 02:03:19.934
fears. How much in your

1900
02:03:20.814 --> 02:03:22.514
experience is it

1901
02:03:23.334 --> 02:03:27.134
other things, the fact that maybe the person who's with that person who's overdosed

1902
02:03:27.494 --> 02:03:31.434
is also currently on drugs, and therefore their cognitive ability to

1903
02:03:31.494 --> 02:03:32.834
assess a situation,

1904
02:03:34.014 --> 02:03:37.684
put in some form of analysis of how severe the case is,

1905
02:03:39.334 --> 02:03:42.774
and that impairment causes some of that delay as well?

1906
02:03:42.794 --> 02:03:46.514
Is there a mix of both things, fear of prosecution as well as

1907
02:03:46.814 --> 02:03:49.994
an ability to have clear thinking at that time?

1908
02:03:53.734 --> 02:03:57.404
I don't have a lot of experience of people saying that directly to me, but I

1909
02:03:57.434 --> 02:04:00.474
understand the point that you're making, that people who

1910
02:04:00.594 --> 02:04:04.114
are affected by drugs

1911
02:04:04.574 --> 02:04:08.394
may have their cognitive abilities impacted in a

1912
02:04:08.434 --> 02:04:10.574
way that will create part of that delay.

1913
02:04:12.474 --> 02:04:16.054
That one is harder for us to create a safe

1914
02:04:19.634 --> 02:04:22.894
response, whereas this one seems to me to be in our

1915
02:04:25.814 --> 02:04:29.634
remit to create safe arrangements for people to

1916
02:04:29.694 --> 02:04:33.274
make that disclosure to get help when they need it.

1917
02:04:33.854 --> 02:04:37.314
And I think that's the opportunity that you have today.

1918
02:04:38.234 --> 02:04:38.574
Thank you.

1919
02:04:40.274 --> 02:04:41.354
Thank you, Dr. Rawiri.

1920
02:04:42.174 --> 02:04:44.824
Appreciate your time. Thank you for your submission. Kia ora.

1921
02:04:45.134 --> 02:04:45.334
Kia ora.

1922
02:04:54.174 --> 02:04:56.894
Next up, we have Tuari Potiki.

