02:05:21.494 --> 02:05:24.414
Mr. Potiki, thank you very much for joining us today.

1926
02:05:24.774 --> 02:05:28.414
We have you here for five minutes. The rules of

1927
02:05:28.454 --> 02:05:31.234
Parliament mean that when hearing your submission, we have to be careful not to

1928
02:05:31.274 --> 02:05:34.394
hear allegations that may seriously damage a person's reputation.

1929
02:05:35.194 --> 02:05:37.134
If you want to leave us time for questions, you may.

1930
02:05:37.214 --> 02:05:40.534
I'll hand that time to you now. Thank you.

1931
02:05:40.594 --> 02:05:42.284
Kia ora. Thank you. Mia kia koutou.

1932
02:05:42.874 --> 02:05:46.374
Kia kite hiana, kia koutou katoa ngā mema o tēnei

1933
02:05:46.554 --> 02:05:49.154
komiti. Tēnā rā koutou. Kia ora. Thank you for the opportunity

1934
02:05:50.314 --> 02:05:52.014
to speak to you this morning.

1935
02:05:53.374 --> 02:05:57.074
I've got three points to make, and hopefully it won't take five whole

1936
02:05:57.154 --> 02:05:58.674
minutes. Firstly,

1937
02:06:01.054 --> 02:06:04.774
when it comes to discretion and fear of punishment

1938
02:06:04.814 --> 02:06:05.954
for

1939
02:06:06.954 --> 02:06:10.274
trying to help somebody who's going through a drug overdose, the

1940
02:06:10.834 --> 02:06:12.674
fear is real. And I think

1941
02:06:13.794 --> 02:06:15.734
one of the points I wanted to make really is that,

1942
02:06:17.274 --> 02:06:21.234
I think Rawiri just alluded to it as well, that police discretion or the

1943
02:06:21.834 --> 02:06:22.354
leaving

1944
02:06:23.334 --> 02:06:25.214
any of it in the hands of police

1945
02:06:26.054 --> 02:06:29.834
doesn't work well for particularly Māori and Pacific New Zealanders.

1946
02:06:31.134 --> 02:06:34.594
We currently have a law that requires police not to prosecute for minor drug

1947
02:06:34.634 --> 02:06:37.394
offenses unless it's in the public good, and

1948
02:06:38.694 --> 02:06:42.574
that law hasn't worked uniformly across New

1949
02:06:42.654 --> 02:06:43.014
Zealand.

1950
02:06:43.934 --> 02:06:47.254
And even where it has worked partially, it hasn't worked for Māori and Pacific.

1951
02:06:47.334 --> 02:06:47.534
So

1952
02:06:48.774 --> 02:06:51.514
Māori and Pacific people are still disproportionately charged and

1953
02:06:51.574 --> 02:06:55.494
convicted of minor drug offenses, and the

1954
02:06:55.534 --> 02:06:57.474
police call this unconscious bias.

1955
02:07:00.674 --> 02:07:02.674
Other people have different names for it.

1956
02:07:02.694 --> 02:07:06.594
But I guess the point I want to make is that the legislation, the

1957
02:07:06.614 --> 02:07:10.514
bill as it progresses through, it's really important that it is clear

1958
02:07:10.594 --> 02:07:11.664
and unambiguous,

1959
02:07:12.494 --> 02:07:16.354
which I think this bill is. I think the more

1960
02:07:16.394 --> 02:07:16.654
that

1961
02:07:18.274 --> 02:07:22.154
the legislation can dictate and guide how people are

1962
02:07:22.214 --> 02:07:26.174
treated, the better. And the less we leave to discretion,

1963
02:07:27.134 --> 02:07:30.274
I think the stronger the bill potentially will be.

1964
02:07:32.194 --> 02:07:36.174
I can't talk to you all without mentioning the

1965
02:07:36.434 --> 02:07:37.754
irony/hypocrisy

1966
02:07:39.134 --> 02:07:42.954
of our current New Zealand policy settings that lead people

1967
02:07:43.494 --> 02:07:47.424
towards the drug that continues to cause the most harm for New Zealanders,

1968
02:07:47.474 --> 02:07:48.234
which is alcohol.

1969
02:07:52.114 --> 02:07:55.694
But we don't talk about alcohol overdose. We have other names for it.

1970
02:07:57.874 --> 02:08:00.094
Even if people die from alcohol use,

1971
02:08:00.954 --> 02:08:02.134
it's called alcohol poisoning,

1972
02:08:03.234 --> 02:08:04.654
not alcohol overdose.

1973
02:08:06.074 --> 02:08:09.954
So I wonder how the attitudes may change

1974
02:08:10.234 --> 02:08:12.574
if we talked about overdose

1975
02:08:14.554 --> 02:08:18.214
for drugs in the same language and called it drug poisoning rather than

1976
02:08:18.414 --> 02:08:21.074
overdose. I think overdose as a word has connotations.

1977
02:08:22.974 --> 02:08:24.654
Maybe that would help shift attitudes-

1978
02:08:26.358 --> 02:08:29.038
And understand it, and situate this issue more

1979
02:08:29.198 --> 02:08:31.538
closely in the health area.

1980
02:08:32.958 --> 02:08:36.158
If we talk about alcohol drug-- sorry, accidental drug poisoning,

1981
