These are carefully targeted protections.

2144
02:17:58.054 --> 02:18:01.575
They're not blanket immunity, nor do they excuse serious

2145
02:18:01.634 --> 02:18:05.034
offending, trafficking, or unrelated criminal conduct.

2146
02:18:05.415 --> 02:18:09.274
They simply ensure that preserving a life is not

2147
02:18:09.314 --> 02:18:12.575
undermined by fear of prosecution for low-level offending.

2148
02:18:13.594 --> 02:18:17.194
Working in medicinal cannabis has shown me the clinical consequences of

2149
02:18:17.274 --> 02:18:20.915
stigma. Detection is not the same as

2150
02:18:20.954 --> 02:18:24.894
causation. The same discipline is required when

2151
02:18:24.934 --> 02:18:28.354
examining an overdose or death. That is

2152
02:18:28.415 --> 02:18:32.335
why this bill matters. Its success should not simply

2153
02:18:32.394 --> 02:18:36.354
be measured by prosecutions, but by whether more people pick

2154
02:18:36.394 --> 02:18:39.774
up the phone without hesitation, stay with the person in

2155
02:18:39.814 --> 02:18:43.114
distress, provide emergency services with honest

2156
02:18:43.175 --> 02:18:47.114
information, and give clinicians the opportunity to intervene

2157
02:18:47.554 --> 02:18:51.454
before an avoidable emergency becomes a preventable death.

