2254
02:24:40.256 --> 02:24:41.746
Yet our current systems

2255
02:24:42.706 --> 02:24:46.486
too often require people in active addiction or

2256
02:24:46.566 --> 02:24:50.556
problematic drug use to wait, make and keep appointments, stay organized, and

2257
02:24:50.626 --> 02:24:54.466
contactable, and prove their readiness before they

2258
02:24:54.485 --> 02:24:58.045
receive any help. This is not realistic for people with severe

2259
02:24:58.206 --> 02:25:01.386
SUDs, and it leaves families trying to hold together the crisis

2260
02:25:02.186 --> 02:25:05.186
that health, justice, and support systems will not meet.

2261
02:25:06.926 --> 02:25:10.226
Severe SUD is characterized by a loss of control.

2262
02:25:11.326 --> 02:25:14.326
Therefore, someone else needs to step in and facilitate sobriety.

2263
02:25:15.426 --> 02:25:19.326
In my son's case, recovery became possible only when he was led to a

2264
02:25:19.406 --> 02:25:21.586
